WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
Why's it gotta be so slow!
*door betrays mark*

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.040
[raspy breathing]

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:02.900
[moaning]

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.100
I'M A BRAVE BOY! *suuuuuuure*

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.600
Hello, everybody! My name is Markiplier,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.600
and welcome to Resident Evil 7

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.600
Now, I've played the demo for this a while back

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.520
and the full game just got released.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.600
I am only going to do NORMAL

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.600
because I'm not a masochist.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.600
[scoffing] Not just gonna start on MADHOUSE

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.600
And, this game promises to be a lot more...

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.080
Hi... Jesus!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.300
Hi~

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.580
...yay...

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.420
...Yea

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:42.780
Hokay

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:44.880
Miss you too!?

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:45.660
...this...

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:56.220
...hoh-kay.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.580
That's so sweet!

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.660
That's so lovely

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.160
Eww.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.580
What's wrong with me?

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:02.720
[whispering] ...what...?

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.180
hiiii...?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.120
HMM.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.360
[Concerned] HHHMMMM.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.720
Okay, so I was wondering.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.600
That cushy baby-sitting job by the sea [phone dialing]

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.200
seemed so bad

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.720
and it was a bit over compensating [ring back tone]

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.360
in the love department.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.040
Me thinks that maybe this lady

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.100
wasn't so faithful to Ethan.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.140
[quietly] Hmm...

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.100
Yeah, okay.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:22.840
Alright.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.040
Man, that's so weird because

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.160
I thought for sure that was live action.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.180
And maybe it's a combination of the two because

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.920
that looks pretty legit out there

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:31.420
like

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.680
not even gonna lie

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.020
that looks legit like film

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.020
but maybe they just ada- OH I UHJU- *Freaking out*

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.420
Do I need to ...?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.420
Oh, I thought I needed to pilot for a second there

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.340
but I guess I'm okay.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.340
Alright, just gonna park in this RANDOM MARSH.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.980
GO LOOK FOR MY WIFE.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.980
I'M THE LOVIN' HUSBAND.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.340
I'm sure nothing BAD's gonna happen

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.140
over here.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:50.340
Oh, cool.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.860
That looks, like, legitimately good.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.160
I'm mean obviously it's a Triple A game

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.940
I don't often get into this so

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.360
of course it's gonna look good.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.260
They made it look good

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.340
and it's current generation.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.660
We're in the future!

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.600
Where graphics are GREAT.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:04.800
Oh man.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:05.860
But I'm excited about this one.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.520
Because this Resident Evil

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.380
promises to be

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.320
pretty darn scary.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.320
Whereas the last two

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.320
have been a little bit, you know

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.840
not quite as scary

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.240
and more action-oriented.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.440
Which is totally fine

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.520
if that's the way they wanted to

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.740
do the game, but

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.060
In *my* opinion

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.060
Resident Evil often offered

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.100
this insight into-

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.740
whoa, that's radical

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.460
offered this insight into this

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.980
zombie apocalypse.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.980
But this one, actually- I don't know if

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.540
it's in a completely different universe

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.540
but it's in, like, this side universe

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.120
where anything can happen.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.480
And I'm willing to bet that I'm

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.520
not gonna be able to get in here

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.080
am I?

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:42.420
Ooh.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:43.320
Menacing.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.600
It rem- [clanging noises, startled pause]

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.560
...H-HI??

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.860
HELLOO?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.900
GOOD DAY

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.460
AH, locked, I see!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.320
Excellent!

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.100
Just testing your security!

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:55.700
Doesn't even seem to be a

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.120
padlock on there.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.380
Just seems to be wrapped around.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.980
Well I wouldn't want to be-[clunking]

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.440
-rude and intrude on anybody's house.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.520
[intercom button click]

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.520
Hello, looking for my wife

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.180
My wife that I assumed is dead.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:10.520
[clanking echoing, ambient noises]

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:11.920
Turns out she's not.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:12.420
Maybe.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.240
ookay.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.260
Alright then.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.760
I'm pretty sure this means, "Keep Out"

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.600
even though I probably could vault over that.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.300
I'll take the [thunk]

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.900
the very dark and dreary path

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.080
off to the side and see where that leads me.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.280
Probably into a world of success

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.240
and NOT death.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.980
Just told me to run but,

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.400
my gamer instincts have already

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.380
taught me otherwise.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.460
[quietly] Now what do we got here...

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.520
[ambient rumbling] Some kind of decrepit van

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.040
Some kind of camera equipment, too.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.780
So it might've been a news van of some sorts.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.020
Now, let's find a dead body!

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.820
Awww, nothin'.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.020
Nuts.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.020
[laughing] "Sewer Gators"?

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.040
"Project Proposal: Sneak into a Louisiana ghost house."

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.020
Oh!

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.020
In the demo there was this

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.760
camera crew that wanted to go around

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:55.980
and look at, like,

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.020
haunted loca- Eeeugh...

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.780
"Join us".

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.960
"Schedule Equipment" ...okay.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.480
And then "Join us" written in

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.980
what I can only assume to be

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.120
cherry red lipstick

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.600
and definitely not blood.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.300
Also why's this tarp here?

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.540
And also why are there wires here?

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:11.760
And also- *wincing*

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.040
"Accept her gift"??

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.420
Whose gift??

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.840
Who we talkin' about here?

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.540
Mia?

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.720
Are we talkin' about Mia?

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:20.060
Are we talking about Mio *mio mio dance *

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:20.960
from Fatal Frame?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.160
[insects buzzing]

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:22.960
[quietly] oh jeeze. Eugch.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.280
Both Ethan and Mark: Eugh.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:25.380
I know right? Gllcgthh

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.080
[footsteps continue]

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.420
Man, this actually, legitimately is really cool

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:29.600
because, I

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.560
It is weird coming from a stance

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.260
where I only play indie horror-

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.240
[tense ambiance undulating]

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.820
What the fffuck--HI??

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:38.460
I

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:38.960
WAS

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:39.460
IN THE MIDDLE

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:39.960
OF HAVING

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:40.460
AN EXISTENTIAL

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.060
CRISIS

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.260
AND THEN you come waltzing

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.120
through the woods!!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:44.680
Uh-uh

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:45.300
Nuh-uh.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.420
Oh no-no.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:47.780
Oh nonono.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.000
Was that a zombo?

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.000
[wet footsteps]

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:50.500
Whadaza

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.860
Was that a zombini?

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.460
[quietly] eeeh...

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.100
Ah, that's definitely a swamp

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.880
At least I know that

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.760
My gamer instincts is telling me

00:05:58.760 --> 00:05:59.880
that I can't go down there.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:00.920
[crows cawing]

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.840
Might as well press onward into this

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.520
infested bog of some sort.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.420
Following some creepy...

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.700
...balding gentleman that might've been a zombie.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.900
Ethan: *gasping*
Mark: Whoa, what the fuck

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.880
is that?

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:12.600
What IS that?

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:13.580
OH WHAT IS THAT

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:14.420
WHAT AM I [crows tumultuate]

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:15.740
Ethan: AAAUGH!
Mark: I DON'T KNOW WHAT I'M LOOKING AT

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.140
...I still don't know what I'm looking at!

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.140
Is that a pair of pants, or is that a dead body?!

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.320
I can hardly tell the two apart!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:23.760
Whewph...

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.500
Whatever that is it dun' look good.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.720
I still... whu [stammers]

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.160
Is my brain just not able to comprehend

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.520
what the hell this is?

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.980
Are those decaying pieces of FLESH

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.400
OR IS THAT A PAIR OF PANTS??

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.700
I legitimately can't tell!

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.980
I'm gonna assume it's flesh.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.120
And NOT the good kind.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.520
...OOHHH IT WAS FLESH

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.320
Oh I shoulda looked to the LEFT

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.120
at the FLESH MONUMENT.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.720
OH GOOD

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.380
OH GREAT

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.360
Wonderful.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.420
Man, I should have-

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.260
I should [sputtering]

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.260
I should PROBABLY go home at this point

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.000
You know

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:55.560
when I see

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:58.420
when I see a Christmas WREATH made of COW LEGS

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.120
I probably don't wanna be around here

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.540
for too much longer.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.980
I mean, the decorative buzz saws

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.480
are definitely an addition, but

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.400
something tells me that only Death awaits down here.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.220
Maybe it's all the Death that's over here.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:12.780
Nah, I think I'll stay crouched.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.220
Just in case, you know.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.220
Just in case that friendly gentleman

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.840
that was walking through the woods

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.640
decides to invite inside

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.980
for a nice Christmas dinner.--

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:22.700
It is good though,  because

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.780
I haven't...[ambient rumbling]

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:25.640
Wwww-Are these the birds that I

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.420
just met over by the questionable

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:28.200
pair of pants??

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.120
Oooh, these are very dead.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:32.360
But why?

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.700
What just killed these things?

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.700
I can only assume it's showing me

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.820
these dead birds because

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:38.680
they *just* died.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.680
They don't look decomposed,

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.020
they don't look eaten.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.020
They're literally the birds that were just over there.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.260
And then they *just died*.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.400
[softly] Oh no.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.060
Is this the back of the house?

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:49.660
The back of the house isn't as meticulously kept

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:51.660
as the blade runner of the house.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.640
[softly] Oh shit.
Ethan: *grunts*

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:54.220
Ah, 'scuze me.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.000
Alrighty then.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:57.520
Hello

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:58.580
Hi.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:07:59.540
How are you?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.700
Examine in detail? Oh I will.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:02.200
Oooh.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:04.860
Is that...

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.360
Is that Mia? [x2]

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.700
Did that say Mia?

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.520
[rustling]

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.600
[quietly] Oh shit.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.480
...Hello.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:12.600
Alright.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.880
What is this?

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.000
Email from Mia.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.780
Print-out of Mia...

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.560
'Kay, let's take a look at this.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.880
"F. Dulvey, Louisiana

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.700
Baker farm. Come get me."

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:25.400
[Confused] But she just recorded a thing

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.400
where she said, "Don't come get me"!

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.580
And it was sent from the future!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.080
I definitely shouldn't trust THIS one

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.300
...Alright, fine. Whatever.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.820
Anything on the back?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.820
No, just an envelope that I haven't [mumbles]

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.080
Man, why does Ethan look like Brendan Fraser there?

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.080
Oh well. Probably a cool guy.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.080
Alright, let's see what we got here.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.240
Mia's driver's licence

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:46.240
covered in a strange black substance.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:48.440
EUH.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:49.640
EUH YA

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:50.600
Ah, that's a good sign [sarcasm]

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:51.100
In my

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.820
In my gaming experience

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.660
when things are covered in a strange black substances

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.660
it's usually the BEST thing that could happen.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:57.780
...ulgck.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.600
[scoffing] Lemme get a closer look

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.480
turns out it's MUD.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:01.860
Alright, what do we got?

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.160
Anything here?

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:04.800
[ambient leaves rustling]

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:06.600
Well, it's definitely Mia Winters.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.020
And this is definitely her purse.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.920
But if this is from three minutes ago

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.920
why would her purse be out here

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.340
in pristine condition?

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.240
like, it's legitimately out here in

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.940
very good condition next to

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:18.700
a burning pile of...whatever.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.080
I have no idea what, though.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.320
[wincing, quietly] oh, we shall see.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:25.940
Hi?

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:27.920
Hello?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.580
Wait, is this the same...?

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.840
Is this the same exact house that we went into before?

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:35.240
They said that the demo didn't have anything to do with the ra-

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.880
the ..[stuttering] the rage game

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.260
the normal game..they said that the demo

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:45.660
